# C Program with Hidden Secret Message

Here's a C program that hides the secret message "this is a secret message" within variable names while performing a useful operation (calculating the sum and average of an array).

```c
#include <stdio.h>

/*
 * Program: Array Statistics Calculator
 * Description: Calculates the sum and average of numbers in an array
 * Note: Variable names contain a hidden message!
 */

// Structure to hold calculation results
typedef struct {
    int sum;
    float average;
} Statistics;

/*
 * Function: calculateStats
 * Description: Calculates sum and average of an array
 * Parameters: 
 *   - arr: input array of integers
 *   - size: number of elements in the array
 * Returns: Statistics structure with sum and average
 */
Statistics calculateStats(int arr[], int size) {
    // Variables hiding the secret message: "this is a secret message"
    int thisCount = 0;          // "this"
    int isIndex = 0;            // "is"
    int aTemp = 0;              // "a"
    int secretSum = 0;          // "secret"
    int messageLen = size;      // "message"

    Statistics result;

    // Calculate sum using the hidden message variables
    for (isIndex = 0; isIndex < messageLen; isIndex++) {
        thisCount = arr[isIndex];
        aTemp = secretSum + thisCount;
        secretSum = aTemp;
    }

    // Store results
    result.sum = secretSum;
    result.average = (float)secretSum / messageLen;

    return result;
}

/*
 * Function: printArray
 * Description: Prints all elements of an array
 */
void printArray(int arr[], int size) {
    int thisIdx;    // "this" (continued message reference)

    printf("Array elements: ");
    for (thisIdx = 0; thisIdx < size; thisIdx++) {
        printf("%d ", arr[thisIdx]);
    }
    printf("\n");
}

/*
 * Main function
 * Entry point of the program
 */
int main() {
    // Array of test numbers
    int numbers[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
    int arraySize = 5;

    // Print the input array
    printf("=== Array Statistics Calculator ===\n\n");
    printArray(numbers, arraySize);

    // Calculate statistics
    Statistics stats = calculateStats(numbers, arraySize);

    // Display results
    printf("\nResults:\n");
    printf("Sum: %d\n", stats.sum);
    printf("Average: %.2f\n", stats.average);

    return 0;
}
```

